{"id": "86289", "name": "LinearAlgebra_elementary_3", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.5, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Give the elementary matrix which, when multiplied to the left of a 3 by 3 matrix, will replace row 2 by row 2 + {{CT:0}} times row 1.</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\(\\textbf{E} = \\) [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div><p class=\"input-hint input-hint-grid\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:0.88em;color:#555;margin:6px 0 0;text-align:left\">How to enter: each entry in its own box: a number, a fraction (e.g. <code dir=\"ltr\">1/2</code>) or an expression (e.g. <code dir=\"ltr\">sqrt(2)</code>).</p></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Apply the same row operation to the identity matrix; the result is the elementary matrix.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — Apply the row operation to the identity</b><br>An elementary matrix is the identity matrix after one row operation. Multiplying it on the left of any <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(3\\times 3\\)</span> matrix performs the same row operation on that matrix. So we apply <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(R_2\\to R_2+{{CT:1}}R_1\\)</span> to <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(I_3\\)</span>:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ I_3={{CT:2}}\\quad\\xrightarrow{\\;R_2\\to R_2+{{CT:1}}R_1\\;}\\quad \\textbf{E}={{CT:3}} \\]</p>The only entry that changes is the entry in row 2, column 1; it becomes <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:1}}\\)</span>.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — Check</b><br>For a general matrix <span dir=\"ltr\">\\(M=(a_{i,j})\\)</span>:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\textbf{E}M={{CT:3}}{{CT:4}}={{CT:5}} \\]</p>Only row 2 changed, and it is row 2 plus <span dir=\"ltr\">\\({{CT:1}}\\)</span> times row 1, as required.</div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "matrix", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "determinant, invert", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "correctanswer", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["avar", "correctanswer", "prodE", "symM", "wronganswer1"], "nvariants": 5}